{
  "$comment": "Names of the languages sf-language supports, from CLDR 48 (ICU 78 as Node.js ships it): each language in itself (native) and in English (en). Since owner decision C282 their names in Russian are the ru language file's words (src/core/js/lang/language-names, name-<code>, registered for sf-language), as any other language's names may be. The browser's Intl.DisplayNames carries fewer languages (headless Chromium names tt only in English and ba, sah not at all; research 2026-11-14-language LG-7), so these names come first and Intl names every other language and page language. Spelled as CLDR writes them; the element gives a name its capital in a list. Data, not code: add a language here with both names, and its Russian name to the language file. Owner decision C278 (2026-11-17): languages of CIS countries other than Russian are not named here (uk, be, uz, az, hy, ka, ky, tg and tk left on 2026-11-18, kk before; tt and ba, languages of regions of Russia, stay); the browser names such a code if a product lists one.",
